    "description": "Search Cognee memory: the permanent knowledge graph of this session's dataset (scope \"graph\", the default), or the indexed repository's code graph (scope \"code\"). Memory is already recalled automatically on every prompt; call this for a deeper or differently worded search, for more results, or to read another dataset by its id. Returns the matching memories as text; an empty result from a reachable server is authoritative."
   },
   {
    "name": "remember",
    "description": "Store what the person asked to remember in Cognee memory (the active dataset's knowledge graph): a preference, a correction, a fact about them, a decision, a note. Use it when they say \"remember this\", \"save this to memory\" or \"store this file\", not on your own initiative: the session is captured automatically, routine tool calls included, so do not store those or your working notes. Category \"user\" for their preferences and facts about them; \"project\" for facts about the codebase, docs and decisions; \"agent\" only when they ask you to keep a finding of yours. Pass \"file\" instead of \"content\" to store a file they named (code then rides the code path). Each call runs a cognify on their key: a session allows 5 calls and 64000 bytes in all; past that the cognee-remember skill is the way."
   }
